# English Code

## Rule

All **new** identifiers must be English:

- Function and variable names
- Signal names
- `class_name` declarations
- New file and folder names under target architecture
- New `res://` paths (`domains/`, `data/`, `presentation/`)

## Legacy exception

Existing Portuguese API (`coletar_save`, `WindowManager`, `aplicar_save`) remains until refactored. Do not mix English aliases for the same function without migration plan.

When touching legacy files:

- New functions/signals: English
- Renaming public API: only with save/version or coordinated refactor

## Save keys

v4 save uses English keys (`gold`, `inventory`) with legacy PT aliases on read — see `docs/architecture/save-format.md`.

## Scenes and resources

- New scenes: `inventory_menu.tscn`, not `menu_inventario.tscn`
- Skill `skill_id` slugs: English preferred for new skills
- Player-visible text still goes through i18n, not English hardcode in UI

## Docs

All documentation (`docs/`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`) is written in **English**. Player-facing UI still uses i18n.

- `docs/conventions/naming.md`
- `docs/architecture/save-format.md` — save key aliases (v4)
